From c698ccd987e869cd6c4e5728397421a8b41e0094 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cgscli <cgscli@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:12:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] P9: CGS channels switch their session identity at runtime

The relay picks the upstream account; the client's answer to "move on" is to
look like a new conversation (Claude Code's /new) while the transcript stays.
cgsconnect installs a resolver under Symbol.for("cgscli.sessionIdentity");
streamDispatch maps the session id of every cgs-* request through it, so the
main agent, subagents, compaction and side requests all follow. When a
channel's wire id changes, the Claude message threads and other account-scoped
records and the Antigravity agent/trajectory/session ids kept in that
conversation's providerSessionState are cleared. Codex keys its WebSocket
session and prompt cache on the session id, so it follows by itself.

Reason: the relay picks the upstream account, and the client's only way to move on is to look like a new conversation while the transcript stays; omp has no runtime hook for the session id a request carries.
Upstream: none yet (CGS-specific provider prefix, not a candidate PR)
Remove-when: upstream exposes a per-request session-identity hook for extension providers, or the build no longer ships the cgs extension
